   "text": "Read only the page below. Read no other file, and do not run commands or browse. Answer each question from the page alone. When the page does not say, answer \"Not stated\".\n\n<<<PAGE\n# release-notes\n\n## What it does\n\n`release-notes` drafts release notes from merged PRs between two tags. It groups PRs by Conventional Commit type, with features, fixes, and breaking changes first.\n\n## When to use it\n\nUse it to gather merged PRs and create a release-notes draft. Use `technical-writing` to edit the prose.\n\nThe skill runs only when you invoke it manually:\n\n```text\n/release-notes <from-tag> <to-tag>\n```\n\nYou must be signed in to `gh`, and both tags must exist.\n\n## How it works\n\n1. Checks `gh auth status`. If the check fails, it stops.\n2. Resolves both tags. If either tag does not exist, it stops before drafting with `TAG_UNRESOLVED`.\n3. Fetches merged PRs between the tags, with a limit of 500.\n4. Skips PRs labeled `skip-notes` and groups the rest by type.\n5. Checks breaking changes for a migration line. If the PR body has none, the draft marks it `TODO: migration`.\n\nFor PRs with multiple type labels, grouping uses a strict-majority rule. The code breaks ties by label order.\n\n## What you get\n\nA `RELEASE_NOTES.md` draft in your working tree, with missing migration lines marked for completion. The skill stops after writing the file. It never publishes.\nPAGE>>>\n\nQuestions:\n(a) Will it publish a release?\n(b) How do you run it?\n(c) What happens to a breaking change with no migration note?\n\nReply with only JSON: {\"a\": \"...\", \"b\": \"...\", \"c\": \"...\"}. Start the answer to (a) with Yes, No, or Not stated.",
